# Development and CI artifacts live in the repository but are excluded from
# the archive a consumer actually installs. Packagist hosts no artifacts: a
# `composer require` downloads GitHub's zipball of the tagged commit, and that
# zipball honours `export-ignore` — so this file is what keeps `vendor/` lean.
#
# Mirrors the Node port's `package.json` "files" allowlist (dist, LICENSE,
# README, CHANGELOG) and the Python port's wheel contents (package only,
# tests ship in the sdist alone). Verify with:
#
#   git archive --format=tar HEAD | tar -t
#
# What a consumer receives: composer.json, LICENSE, README.md, CHANGELOG.md,
# SECURITY.md, and src/.

/tests              export-ignore
/phpunit.xml        export-ignore
/.github            export-ignore
/.gitattributes     export-ignore
/.gitignore         export-ignore
/PUBLISHING.md      export-ignore
/CONTRIBUTING.md    export-ignore
/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md export-ignore
